course: dictionary
lesson: 9215
title: The longest and shortest days
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The Sun does not stay at the same height in the sky all year. A solstice is one of the two days each year when the Sun is at its highest or lowest point at noon. «At an equinox day and night are about equal; at the summer solstice, about 21 June in the north, we have the longest day.»
explain: Look at the words around solstice to find its meaning. The sentence compares it with equinox, where day and night are about equal, so a solstice must be different: one day is extra long or extra short. The summer solstice has the longest daylight, and the winter solstice has the shortest.
explain: «Astronomers (scientists who study the sky) start the seasons at the equinoxes and solstices: spring at about 20 March, summer at the longest day, about 21 June.» The brackets explain astronomers, and the dates show that a solstice is a fixed day in the year, not a season.
fact: A solstice is one of two days each year.
fact: A solstice is when the Sun is at its highest or lowest point in the sky at noon.
fact: Solstices happen because the Earth's axis is tilted.
fact: In the Northern Hemisphere, the summer solstice is around 21 June and the winter solstice is around 21 December; in Australia and New Zealand it is the other way round.
fact: Stonehenge and Newgrange in Ireland line up with the solstice sun.
exercise: «At the summer solstice, about 21 June in the north, we have the longest day.» On which date does the summer solstice fall in the north? | About 21 December | About 25 December | About 20 March | *About 21 June
exercise: What is a solstice? | A day when day and night are exactly equal | A dark night with no moon | A kind of cloud | *One of the two days each year when the Sun is at its highest or lowest point at noon
exercise: Which solstice has the shortest daylight? | The equinox | The summer solstice | *The winter solstice
test: Using the brackets in the text, what is an equinox? | *A day when the Sun is at its highest point | A day when day and night are about equal | A type of star | The longest day of the year
test: «In Australia and New Zealand, the solstices are the other way round.» When is the summer solstice in Australia? | *Around 21 December | Around 21 September | Around 21 June | Around 20 March
exam: «Astronomers start the seasons at the equinoxes and solstices: summer at the longest day, about 21 June.» According to this, what marks the start of summer? | *The summer solstice, the longest day | The equinox in March | The first frost of autumn | The winter solstice in December
